        "header": "4Method",
        "images": [
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2610.09920/2610.09920v1/fig2_method.png",
                "caption": "Figure 2:The three steps of the attack.Flames: models the attacker trains for an encoderEE; snowflakes: frozen models, which at inference include all of them. Step 0 identifiesEEfrom the stored index with public encoders alone (§4.2); step 1 trains models forEEon public pages; in step 2, each row shows, per storage configuration, where the page shape and the order come from. The inverter uses its ordered variant when the order is known and its set variant otherwise (§4.1).",
                "position": 404
            }
        ]
    },
